{
  "Version": 2,
  "Name": "Epstein1952-bandpass-490-580",
  "Source": "L. I. Epstein, \"The Design of Optical Filters,\" J. Opt. Soc. Am. 42, 806-810 (1952). doi:10.1364/JOSA.42.000806 - Table III (p.809), design described in the text pp.809-810",
  "Notes": "Band-pass filter (pass band 490-580 nm) made of two periodically stratified media of symmetrical periods: A = four periods of MgF2/ZnS/MgF2 (2phi_p = phi_q = 110.8 deg) on the glass side and B = four periods of ZnS/MgF2/ZnS (2phi_p = phi_q = 67.9 deg) on the air side, with one period of MgF2/ZnS/MgF2 (2phi_p = phi_q = 135 deg) as antireflection coating between glass and A\nSpecification: Pass band 490-580 nm; high reflectance on both sides (A reflects 580-803 nm, B reflects 354-490 nm).\nReported: Fig. 6 (calculated reflectance 300-800 nm, 10 % grid; read off the plot, approximate): R ~ 90-100 % with ripple from ~345 to ~445 nm, falls to ~50 % at 490 nm, minimum R ~ 0 at ~520 nm, R < 10 % roughly 505-548 nm, ~70 % at 580 nm, then ~95-100 % from ~600 to ~790 nm (~93 % at 800 nm). Vertical lines at 490 and 580 nm mark the desired pass band. Text p.810: first-order high-reflectance band of A extends from 580 to 803 nm and that of B from 354 to 490 nm; the Herpin index of B equals that of air at 540 nm; the indices of A and B are equal at 516 nm (Fig. 5); A has equivalent index 0.595 at 544 nm, and the AR period (1) with 2phi_p = phi_q = 135 deg has index (1.52 x 0.595)^0.5 = 0.95 at 544 nm. Sum of the printed optical thicknesses = 1698.6 deg at 546 nm = 18.873 QWOT.\nNotes: Table III lists the layers from the glass (1.52, massive) to air (1.00, massive); they are reversed here so layer 1 is next to air. Thicknesses are optical thicknesses at 546 nm in degrees of phase (90 deg = one quarter wave), converted to QWOT = deg/90 at reference_nm 546 and rounded to 6 decimals. 20 layers as printed: AR period 67.3 L / 134.5 H with its outer L merged into A's first L (122.7 = 67.3 + 55.4), then A (7 layers of 110.8 deg, ending with a half-layer L 55.4), then B (H 33.9, 7 layers of 67.9 deg, H 33.9) facing air with no AR coating; the indices alternate 1.38/2.30 except at the A/B junction (L 55.4 next to H 33.9). Indices 2.30 (ZnS) and 1.38 (MgF2) are non-dispersive, as in the paper. Normal incidence from air; a lossless stack reflects equally from either side, and the paper's curve ignores the back surface of the glass (semi-infinite n = 1.52). Total of printed optical thicknesses: 1698.6 deg.\nLayers from Table III (p.809), design described in the text pp.809-810; layer 1 faces the incident medium.\nChecked with ThinFilmDesigner (2026-10-21), agrees with the paper: ours R 44.4 % at 490 nm, minimum 0.175 % at 521 nm, 69.4 % at 580 nm; paper Fig. 6: ~50 % at 490 nm, ~0 at ~520 nm, ~70 % at 580 nm.",
